## 1. `captureFrame()` signature and threading

**Signature:** `Future<Uint8List>` — async, not synchronous.

Abstract contract:

```17:17:/Users/jace/Documents/newapp/packages/core/core_visual_stream/lib/src/visual_stream.dart
  Future<Uint8List> captureFrame();
```

**`MediaKitVisualStream` implementation:** awaits `_player.screenshot()` on the main async flow; no `compute()`, no `Isolate`, no background thread usage anywhere in `core_visual_stream`.

```85:96:/Users/jace/Documents/newapp/packages/core/core_visual_stream/lib/src/media_kit_visual_stream.dart
  Future<Uint8List> captureFrame() async {
    final bytes = await _player.screenshot(format: 'image/png');
    if (bytes == null || bytes.isEmpty) {
      debugPrint('[VisualStream][MediaKit] captureFrame failed: empty screenshot');
      throw const AppError(
        code: 'VISUAL_STREAM_CAPTURE_FAILED',
        message: 'Unable to capture a frame from the visual stream.',
      );
    }
    debugPrint('[VisualStream][MediaKit] captureFrame bytes=${bytes.length}');
    return bytes;
  }
```

Grep across `packages/core/core_visual_stream` finds no `compute` or `Isolate`. It runs as a normal async method (likely on the UI isolate, depending on `media_kit` internals).

