## 3. `sessionId` lifecycle (refresh, new screenshot, background/resume)

The UI wires two different actions:

```82:84:/Users/jace/Documents/newapp/packages/feature/ai/feature_glasses_object_recognition/lib/src/view/object_recognition_page.dart
              onNewFrame: controller.newRecognition,
              onCancel: controller.cancelAnswer,
              onRefresh: controller.refreshLast,
```

**Refresh (`refreshLast`):** Re-asks the last question with **no new screenshot** and **reuses `sessionId`**.

```156:160:/Users/jace/Documents/newapp/packages/feature/ai/feature_glasses_object_recognition/lib/src/viewmodel/object_recognition_controller.dart
  Future<void> refreshLast() async {
    final question = _lastQuestion;
    if (question == null || question.isEmpty || state.isBusy) return;
    await ask(question);
  }
```

`ask()` only captures when `newFrame || imageUrls.isEmpty`:

```94:95:/Users/jace/Documents/newapp/packages/feature/ai/feature_glasses_object_recognition/lib/src/viewmodel/object_recognition_controller.dart
    var imageUrls = state.imageUrls;
    if (newFrame || imageUrls.isEmpty) {
```

So refresh keeps existing `imageUrls` and passes `state.sessionId` into `ask()` — **no new `sessionId` is created client-side**.

**New screenshot (`newRecognition`):** Captures a new frame and uploads, but **still reuses existing `sessionId`** when calling the API.

```162:166:/Users/jace/Documents/newapp/packages/feature/ai/feature_glasses_object_recognition/lib/src/viewmodel/object_recognition_controller.dart
  Future<void> newRecognition() async {
    final question = state.inputText.trim().isEmpty ? '这是什么？' : state.inputText.trim();
    state = state.copyWith(inputText: '');
    await ask(question, newFrame: true);
  }
```

`sessionId` is:
- Initially `null` in state
- Updated from server deltas (`answerDelta` / `done`) in `_handleAnswerDelta` (lines 249, 251)
- Cleared only in `clearHistory()` (line 207)
- **Never explicitly reset** on refresh or new frame

There is **no app background/resume handling** in this feature: no `WidgetsBindingObserver`, no `AppLifecycleState`, no lifecycle-specific session logic. Grep in `feature_glasses_object_recognition` finds nothing for lifecycle/resume.

